WEBVTT

00:11.910 --> 00:18.210
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

01:30.320 --> 01:35.910
#47: THE MIRACULOUS LIGHT BOASTS ITS GLORY
FOR JUST ONE MOMENT

01:39.410 --> 01:41.250
Hey, what's your problem?!

01:41.620 --> 01:43.370
Don't just stand there! Lift me up!

01:44.080 --> 01:47.500
I believe someone is causing
some mess around here.

01:47.500 --> 01:49.210
You know where she went?

01:49.210 --> 01:52.010
Who gives a crap?!
Just help me already!

01:52.570 --> 01:54.320
Well...

01:54.900 --> 01:57.180
Know any good dessert cafes nearby?

01:57.180 --> 01:59.850
I could dig for a matcha frappe right now.

01:59.850 --> 02:02.270
Huh?! Are you going senile, old man?!

02:02.270 --> 02:05.480
Did you break out of
a nursing home or something?!

02:06.650 --> 02:07.900
Impressive.

02:07.900 --> 02:13.650
Running on SLF technology and all that,
they properly react to irrelevant stuff.

02:14.280 --> 02:15.320
There.

02:21.290 --> 02:22.710
You saved me.

02:23.710 --> 02:26.080
Guess I gotta thank you, old man.

02:26.830 --> 02:29.130
If you're looking for
a monster running amok,

02:29.130 --> 02:32.670
she went down to that alley
after pushing me off this building.

02:33.160 --> 02:34.720
That's all I know.

02:35.040 --> 02:36.970
I see. Thanks.

02:36.970 --> 02:39.970
HEROIC GAUGE

02:39.970 --> 02:44.140
The core element of this
Galaxia Heroes fighting game

02:44.140 --> 02:49.400
lies not only in its fights but also
in its Hero versus Villain dynamic.

02:50.330 --> 02:54.820
By role-playing the characters
from Galaxia Comic,

02:55.190 --> 02:58.830
you can dash across the skyscrapers
at night like a superhero,

02:58.830 --> 03:02.450
or wreck havoc all you want
like your favorite villain.

03:02.910 --> 03:06.250
This game is made to let you
live up to that fantasy.

03:07.500 --> 03:11.630
In the previous installments, those mechanics
were merely a little extra spice,

03:11.630 --> 03:16.220
but thanks to the SLF tech,
it now lets you do all kinds of things.

03:16.220 --> 03:19.430
So in essence, Galaxia Heroes: Chaos,

03:19.430 --> 03:24.310
is more of a simulation
than a fighting game.

03:24.920 --> 03:29.230
I bet this game is the best game ever
for the fans of the Galaxia Comics.

03:29.230 --> 03:30.150
HERO - VILLAIN

03:30.150 --> 03:32.820
HERO - VILLAIN
The Heroic Gauge and Villanic Gauge

03:32.820 --> 03:35.150
HERO - VILLAIN
are designed to fill up more

03:35.150 --> 03:37.660
HEROIC GAUGE - VILLANIC GAUGE
as players enact their characters.

03:37.660 --> 03:39.740
HEROIC GAUGE - VILLANIC GAUGE
And by consuming that,

03:39.740 --> 03:43.620
HEROIC GAUGE - VILLANIC GAUGE
they can unleash Specials or Super Finishers.

03:44.010 --> 03:47.540
From that fact alone,
you can tell role-playing is recommended.

03:47.540 --> 03:51.500
But these gauges
have one more key function.

03:51.500 --> 03:52.020
CHAOS CUBE

03:52.020 --> 03:54.170
CHAOS CUBE
The existence of the Chaos Cube

03:54.170 --> 03:55.420
CHAOS CUBE
you can obtain by consuming

03:55.420 --> 03:57.940
CHAOS CUBE
all your gauge when it's at max.

03:57.940 --> 04:00.010
CHAOS CUBE
The winning condition in this game

04:00.010 --> 04:02.260
CHAOS CUBE
is to either defeat the other player

04:02.260 --> 04:04.520
CHAOS CUBE
or obtain a Chaos Cube.

04:05.220 --> 04:09.650
The Chaos Cubes are set in random
locations within the battlefield.

04:09.650 --> 04:11.560
And if you're aiming to obtain one,

04:11.560 --> 04:16.570
in theory, you can win the match
without ever fighting your opponent.

04:16.570 --> 04:19.410
That's where strategy comes in.

04:20.490 --> 04:25.200
Whether you fight or not,
role-playing is a must.

04:25.910 --> 04:27.290
I see.

04:27.710 --> 04:30.830
No wonder Katzo was so persistent
in telling us to read the comics.

04:30.830 --> 04:34.670
The more you know about the character,
the clearer your approach to battle is.

04:39.590 --> 04:42.800
So, what's your character again?

04:43.300 --> 04:46.060
I think she got kidnapped by Mad Doctor

04:46.460 --> 04:50.560
and obtained the power to control
plants after surgery.

04:51.520 --> 04:53.060
Her name was...

04:53.560 --> 04:56.490
Yggdrya, was it?

04:58.640 --> 04:59.950
Yggdrya.

04:59.950 --> 05:01.530
A woman that kidnapped by Mad Doctor

05:01.530 --> 05:03.240
and had her body modified,

05:03.240 --> 05:05.870
giving her the power to control plants.

05:05.870 --> 05:08.000
A mid-range low-mobility character

05:08.000 --> 05:10.460
specialized in trap and counter moves.

05:10.460 --> 05:13.170
A self-absorbed woman lacking in morals

05:13.170 --> 05:15.670
showing no qualms in despicable acts.

05:15.670 --> 05:17.760
She won't hesitate to do anything

05:17.760 --> 05:20.340
as long as it makes her happy.

05:20.710 --> 05:22.760
And you're playing Ranzo.

05:22.760 --> 05:25.680
A samurai specialized in close combat.

05:25.680 --> 05:28.470
You picked a quite simple character.
Color me surprised.

05:30.980 --> 05:34.310
Let's have you show it, then...

05:35.060 --> 05:36.860
Show me how skilled you really are!

05:38.150 --> 05:39.690
Trap Seed!

05:45.830 --> 05:47.240
Too easy.

05:48.120 --> 05:52.120
One of Yggdrya's trap moves that'll
immobilize you and turn you into a sandbag

05:52.120 --> 05:54.430
for a few seconds if you get hit by it.

05:55.040 --> 05:59.210
But because it can only go straight
once they're launched,

05:59.210 --> 06:01.050
dodging them is a piece of cake!

06:05.890 --> 06:08.890
She timed her attack right
when it'll be difficult to evade.

06:08.890 --> 06:11.520
So she already anticipated
I'd be able to dodge her traps?!

06:13.520 --> 06:14.730
He deflected it?!

06:19.110 --> 06:20.990
Um, what was it again?

06:20.990 --> 06:24.820
"Let me show you the art
of my Ramba style," right?

06:26.570 --> 06:28.830
RANKI STYLE: MICHIYUKI

06:31.080 --> 06:35.170
The special movement skill that lets you
traverse roughly five meters instantly!

06:35.170 --> 06:38.340
Now you're within my range!

06:39.210 --> 06:41.460
VILLANIC GAUGE
I got you!

06:49.890 --> 06:51.560
Super Finisher:

06:51.560 --> 06:54.350
SUPER FINISHER: GREEN GROUND ZERO
Green Ground Zero.

06:54.350 --> 06:57.360
I timed it with your
"Ranki Style: Michiyuki" animation.

06:57.360 --> 06:59.360
You can't avoid taking a lot of damage!

06:59.360 --> 07:00.690
Whoa!

07:00.690 --> 07:04.320
"Old Bones Onslaught"
lets you jump this high?

07:04.820 --> 07:07.320
OLD BONES ONSLAUGHT

07:07.320 --> 07:09.950
No way...
You dodged that?

07:09.950 --> 07:12.660
Your timing was perfect.

07:12.660 --> 07:15.210
It would've been a direct hit
if I didn't see it coming.

07:15.650 --> 07:19.210
But if I expected it coming from the start,
it's not all that hard to deal with.

07:21.250 --> 07:24.590
Now, how should I cut you up?

07:24.590 --> 07:26.090
HEROIC GAUGE
Super Finisher:

07:26.090 --> 07:27.090
HEROIC GAUGE

07:28.890 --> 07:29.800
Amatsukaze...

07:31.100 --> 07:33.020
Windstorm Slash!

07:34.730 --> 07:37.850
SUPER FINISHER:
AMATSUKAZE WINDSTORM SLASH

07:39.110 --> 07:40.610
You're taking it head-on, eh?

07:42.360 --> 07:43.860
YGGDRYA

07:43.860 --> 07:46.240
I can win this!
I just need one more swing!

07:53.410 --> 07:57.040
You purposely took the hit
and pretended to get hurt,

07:57.040 --> 07:59.290
all to give me the space
to pursue you, didn't you?

07:59.920 --> 08:02.210
That's some nice damage control.

08:02.210 --> 08:04.670
And to commit to it so seamlessly...

08:04.670 --> 08:06.720
That's a pro gamer for you.

08:06.720 --> 08:08.800
Well done.

08:08.800 --> 08:10.020
But...

08:10.970 --> 08:14.940
Since I know you were aiming
for a counter, it was all for nothing!

08:18.020 --> 08:21.190
I suppose it wasn't
a bad strategy for Yggdrya.

08:21.610 --> 08:23.610
But by the end of the day,

08:23.610 --> 08:27.000
a fighting game is a game where you
deplete your opponent's health.

08:27.000 --> 08:28.950
If you keep playing passively,

08:29.610 --> 08:33.280
you'll let your opponent
have the initiative, Natsume.

08:35.200 --> 08:37.710
You're giving advice to a pro?

08:37.710 --> 08:39.580
You and your little mouth.

08:39.580 --> 08:41.020
Sunraku.

08:42.960 --> 08:45.250
GALAXIA HEROES: CHAOS.

08:45.670 --> 08:46.960
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

08:47.510 --> 08:50.050
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

08:50.050 --> 08:52.090
GALAXIA HEROES: CHAOS.

08:58.600 --> 09:00.600
I exhausted my Villanic Gauge.

09:00.600 --> 09:02.610
Doing this eats it up
faster than I expected.

09:05.480 --> 09:06.980
Oh, she's running?

09:07.500 --> 09:10.360
She must be planning
to fill her gauge back up.

09:10.360 --> 09:12.990
I see. I'm starting
to get how her game works.

09:13.490 --> 09:16.990
Take the initiative and fight at your
own tempo to keep the advantage.

09:16.990 --> 09:19.500
That's Natsume's battle style, huh?

09:19.500 --> 09:24.880
She lays low, observes her opponent's movement,
and grasps what action they'd make.

09:26.630 --> 09:29.170
If she can take the fight flow
in her tempo,

09:29.170 --> 09:31.510
she can turn disadvantageous
situations around,

09:31.510 --> 09:34.760
and seize back the initiative
from her opponent in an instant.

09:35.170 --> 09:38.220
So that's why she picked
a counter-focused character, huh?

09:39.850 --> 09:42.270
Katzo and Pencilgon
are in that camp as well.

09:42.270 --> 09:44.020
That's why I know.

09:44.020 --> 09:45.560
For types like them...

09:46.400 --> 09:49.530
Nothing annoys them more
than getting their rhythm broken!

09:51.360 --> 09:52.490
His sword?!

09:52.490 --> 09:54.320
Ranki Style: Michiyuki.

09:57.870 --> 09:59.950
My gauge isn't back to full yet.

09:59.950 --> 10:05.130
This Sunraku guy is the type
who persistently sticks to his own pattern.

10:05.130 --> 10:08.590
No matter what opponent he faces,
he fights in the way he wants.

10:08.590 --> 10:11.420
The most annoying kind to fight
once they get on a roll!

10:11.420 --> 10:14.930
I must win back the initiative, too!

10:16.510 --> 10:17.180
Super Finisher:

10:18.010 --> 10:20.060
Amatsukaze Windstorm Slash!

10:21.100 --> 10:24.020
He's forcing me to make decisions
over and over again!

10:25.810 --> 10:29.150
The moment I can't deal
with every one of them, I lose.

10:29.690 --> 10:31.780
His battle style changes
at the drop of a hat!

10:32.700 --> 10:36.160
I know this...
His fighting style is just like...

10:36.780 --> 10:38.100
Silvia's!

10:38.780 --> 10:40.950
Silvia Goldberg!

10:53.050 --> 10:56.180
Judging from that expression,
you lost didn't you, Meg?

10:56.560 --> 10:58.800
He started moving like a maniac midway!

10:58.800 --> 11:01.520
He kept taunting me
like he was mocking my strategy.

11:01.520 --> 11:02.680
What's wrong with him?

11:02.680 --> 11:04.730
Yeah, I get that.

11:04.730 --> 11:06.190
Annoying, wasn't it?

11:06.190 --> 11:07.560
But he's strong.

11:08.520 --> 11:12.570
Although only briefly,
he reminds me of Silvia.

11:13.280 --> 11:15.700
You felt it too, huh?

11:15.700 --> 11:19.580
I hate to admit it,
but he's capable, I'll give him that.

11:19.970 --> 11:22.890
By using and mixing
every trick in the book,

11:22.890 --> 11:25.580
he forces you to make difficult decisions
one after another.

11:26.170 --> 11:30.670
He's like a Swiss army knife
where his every move can kill you.

11:32.050 --> 11:35.340
You can beat him with
the right killer pattern,

11:35.340 --> 11:38.970
but somehow, I only have like
a 60% win rate against him.

11:38.970 --> 11:40.800
60%?!

11:40.800 --> 11:44.270
You, Kei Uomi, a guy whose
winning percentage has never gone

11:44.270 --> 11:46.060
below 80% in official matches?

11:46.060 --> 11:48.900
Hmm, I take it back.
It was more like 70%.

11:48.900 --> 11:51.270
N-No wonder he's so strong.

11:52.020 --> 11:56.860
But Sunraku's mind is completely
obsessed with seeking fun over all else.

11:56.860 --> 11:59.700
His play lacks stability at times.

12:00.910 --> 12:05.410
But their play styles certainly
overlap in some areas.

12:06.790 --> 12:09.170
Maybe I should try that out.

12:09.170 --> 12:09.860
Huh?

12:09.860 --> 12:11.460
Ah, never mind.

12:11.460 --> 12:15.090
Oh, yeah, did you play with Pen—
Towa Amane, yet?

12:15.090 --> 12:16.720
Well, she said...

12:16.720 --> 12:19.050
I wanted to test something
out with Sunraku!

12:19.050 --> 12:22.760
And she went off to have a match
against Sunraku first.

12:22.760 --> 12:25.810
Is she also as good as him?

12:25.810 --> 12:28.280
Hmm... Not sure how to describe her.

12:28.280 --> 12:30.600
It's not a matter of being good or bad,

12:30.600 --> 12:31.770
she's more like, evil—

12:31.770 --> 12:33.150
That's dirty!

12:33.150 --> 12:34.690
That's so goddamn dirty, dammit!

12:35.170 --> 12:36.990
Oh, I'm sorry.

12:36.990 --> 12:40.610
I never paid attention
to the cries of sore losers.

12:40.610 --> 12:42.700
You monster! Demon! Fiend!

12:42.700 --> 12:45.580
I can't quite tell what you're saying.

12:45.580 --> 12:49.670
Judging by that exchange,
Sunraku fell into your trap, huh?

12:49.670 --> 12:51.500
What? Sunraku lost?

12:52.500 --> 12:55.250
Guys! You have to listen
to how low-down this woman is!

12:55.250 --> 13:00.260
She started playing Jenga with a building
with thousands of NPCs inside!

13:00.260 --> 13:01.540
What a monster.

13:01.540 --> 13:03.470
W-Why would you do that?

13:03.470 --> 13:06.140
Because Sunraku would need
to help those swarms of NPCs,

13:06.140 --> 13:08.560
and while he was busy doing that...

13:09.810 --> 13:12.190
...I just squashed him like a bug!

13:12.190 --> 13:14.320
See what I mean? Evil.

13:14.320 --> 13:16.780
I-I see.

13:17.480 --> 13:21.660
Now, let's hear your impressions
of the game so far.

13:22.060 --> 13:24.410
It's like a sandbox
or a tower offense game.

13:24.410 --> 13:26.490
For the Villain characters, at least.

13:26.490 --> 13:30.710
It's like a one-against-many sim
with some battle elements tacked on.

13:30.710 --> 13:33.960
Um, it offers a high degree of freedom,

13:33.960 --> 13:37.000
so you need to plan your actions
over a wide range...

13:37.000 --> 13:41.190
Wait, are you asking me
to give some interesting take, too?

13:42.370 --> 13:46.970
Don't worry about it. Their neurons are
just bugged out, there's no fix for that.

13:47.430 --> 13:49.270
You're fine the way you are, Meg.

13:51.270 --> 13:53.100
Y-You think so?

13:53.100 --> 13:56.980
So you like me the way
I am right now, huh?

13:56.980 --> 13:59.610
Did you feel that, Sunraku?

13:59.610 --> 14:02.360
Yes, of course, Miss Pencil.

14:02.360 --> 14:05.780
This is totally a case of a clueless
protagonist who never notices the obvious.

14:05.780 --> 14:08.620
Tch, it makes me wanna give him
the middle finger with a smile.

14:08.620 --> 14:12.290
Huh? I have no idea what you're saying,
but I know you're dissing me.

14:13.170 --> 14:14.540
Well, whatever.

14:14.540 --> 14:16.500
With those in mind,

14:16.500 --> 14:20.170
let's discuss our proper plan
against Star Rain.

14:20.170 --> 14:22.340
Or so I was thinking,
but before that...

14:22.820 --> 14:24.340
Sunraku, you got a moment?

14:24.340 --> 14:25.090
Huh?

14:25.590 --> 14:28.350
Let's have a match.
You and me.

14:28.350 --> 14:29.970
Oh, you're on!

14:30.370 --> 14:33.320
There are still a lot of characters
I haven't tried out in PVP.

14:33.320 --> 14:34.810
Maybe I should try out a Villain—

14:34.810 --> 14:35.350
No.

14:35.980 --> 14:38.360
I'd like you to play Metius for me.

14:38.360 --> 14:39.860
METIUS
What?

14:40.200 --> 14:43.950
And I'll go all out to crush you.

14:43.950 --> 14:47.830
So you better come at me
just as seriously, Sunraku.

14:48.370 --> 14:50.620
Because otherwise,
there's no point in this.

14:51.410 --> 14:52.600
Kei?

14:53.680 --> 14:56.630
Heh, how long has it been...

14:57.170 --> 15:00.630
...since we competed in a fighting game
with no bugs involved?

15:00.630 --> 15:02.550
Sure thing, Katzo.

15:02.550 --> 15:03.880
Let's do this seriously.

15:20.270 --> 15:23.240
HERO VERSUS HERO MATCH ESTABLISHED
Hero versus Hero match established.

15:23.240 --> 15:25.530
SUNRAKU VS K
Sunraku versus K.

15:33.910 --> 15:35.660
METIUS
PLAYER: SUNRAKU

15:37.750 --> 15:40.670
Just as you wished, Katzo,
I'm gonna fight for real!

15:42.050 --> 15:43.460
I'm playing as Metius.

15:43.460 --> 15:46.090
He's a character who traverses the field

15:46.090 --> 15:48.840
in all dimensions with his midair jumps,
wall runs, and so on.

15:48.840 --> 15:52.100
A close-range attacker
boasting top-class mobility.

15:57.170 --> 16:00.740
The troubling part about him is that
he needs to do a full stop to make a turn

16:00.740 --> 16:02.920
and that he doesn't
pack a lot of punch.

16:03.480 --> 16:06.240
Is that an NPC Villain?

16:06.240 --> 16:08.110
NPC Villain.

16:08.110 --> 16:15.160
During Hero versus Hero matches,
they are placed on the field as NPCs.

16:21.040 --> 16:23.300
HEROIC GAUGE
Oh, thank you so much.

16:23.300 --> 16:25.170
HEROIC GAUGE

16:25.170 --> 16:26.970
Don't mind it.

16:34.680 --> 16:37.940
But man, moving midair sure feels nice.

16:38.330 --> 16:41.900
It'd be awesome if I could
bring this over into SLF.

16:42.400 --> 16:43.070
Hm?

16:43.070 --> 16:44.980
There he is.

16:44.980 --> 16:48.360
Better not dwell on building
gauge and just attack him.

16:48.360 --> 16:49.820
Which character did Katzo pick?

16:50.820 --> 16:52.870
That is...

16:52.870 --> 16:55.080
The Hero character Armed Lava, right?

16:55.080 --> 16:56.660
Armed lava.

16:56.660 --> 16:58.330
His arms are made out of lava,

16:58.330 --> 17:00.670
letting him craft Liquid-Metal Bolts

17:00.670 --> 17:03.210
by melting concrete and steel.

17:03.210 --> 17:04.590
The range of his bolts is only

17:04.590 --> 17:05.800
four or five meters at best.

17:06.220 --> 17:10.000
The type that's strong up close,
but weak against mid-ranged foes.

17:10.000 --> 17:12.800
A character leaning more toward
being a close-range fighter, huh?

17:13.260 --> 17:16.520
Doesn't look like he's trying
to compete on mobility.

17:16.520 --> 17:19.180
Does he want to brawl it out up close?

17:19.640 --> 17:23.400
He asked me to play Metius for him.

17:23.400 --> 17:26.070
I don't know what kind
of scheme he has for me,

17:26.980 --> 17:31.200
but the bigger problem is that
he beat me more than I beat him.

17:31.580 --> 17:33.320
Of course, I'll go all out!

17:33.700 --> 17:36.580
I'll make you pay for all
the humiliation over in BERP!

17:36.580 --> 17:38.200
Star Road!

17:38.200 --> 17:41.460
Well then, I hope this gives me my answer.

17:41.460 --> 17:45.520
Hey! I'm here to play with you, Katzo!

17:46.710 --> 17:48.090
ARMED LAVA

17:49.590 --> 17:51.090
METIUS
PLAYER: SUNRAKU

17:52.340 --> 17:55.350
One of Armed Lava's unique traits,
the Lava Armor, huh?

17:55.350 --> 17:57.180
Although limited to only his arms,

17:57.180 --> 17:59.850
he can deal damage
to any foe he touches with it.

17:59.850 --> 18:02.950
I'm sure you tried to sneak in an attack
somewhere besides my arms,

18:02.950 --> 18:05.810
but the sparkly sound effects he makes
when he's running are loud,

18:05.810 --> 18:09.110
so Metius is not a good
character for stealth.

18:09.110 --> 18:12.110
Metius's main means of
attack are with his legs.

18:12.490 --> 18:14.570
If they're blocked by his Lava Armor,

18:14.570 --> 18:18.120
my legs will naturally be the part
that gets damaged over time.

18:18.120 --> 18:22.660
If I keep attacking him mindlessly,
it'll kill my mobility sooner or later.

18:22.660 --> 18:24.620
I'm well aware!

18:25.880 --> 18:27.460
The best approach here...

18:27.460 --> 18:30.210
...is a hit-and-run
while dodging his arms!

18:33.590 --> 18:36.470
You can react precisely
even at this speed?

18:36.470 --> 18:39.890
This bastard. Our characters
couldn't be a worse match.

18:39.890 --> 18:42.310
This is what he wanted
to test out, isn't it?

18:42.690 --> 18:44.350
Liquid-Metal Bolts.

18:44.810 --> 18:48.070
Unless I deal with those,
he won't let me touch him, eh?

18:48.070 --> 18:50.570
Fine by me! I'll play your game!

18:50.950 --> 18:53.950
I will run straight, build up my
speed, and charge right through!

18:53.950 --> 18:57.450
You ain't gonna hit me
that easily, Katzo!

18:57.450 --> 18:59.200
Go ahead!
Try dodging this, Sunraku!

18:59.990 --> 19:03.080
Five meters! I'm in range
of his Liquid-Metal Bolts!

19:03.960 --> 19:05.710
He's still not firing?
Is he bluffing?

19:06.080 --> 19:09.880
Three meters...
No, he definitely crafted a new bolt.

19:09.880 --> 19:11.710
He oughta be able to shoot.

19:11.710 --> 19:13.170
One meter...

19:13.170 --> 19:16.390
He changed his stance?
Is he trying to parry me?

19:16.390 --> 19:18.850
Either way, Katzo, you screwed up!

19:18.850 --> 19:20.680
If I'm this close up to you,

19:20.680 --> 19:24.180
I can smash your side with my leg
faster than you can react!

19:25.350 --> 19:26.850
Wait, no...

19:26.850 --> 19:30.110
His real aim was to attack from the left!

19:30.110 --> 19:31.480
Liquid-Metal Bolt.

19:32.480 --> 19:34.490
LIQUID-METAL BOLT

19:35.750 --> 19:36.860
You're kidding me...

19:37.660 --> 19:40.740
He forcefully went from his kicking
animation to bending backward!

19:40.740 --> 19:43.500
You can actually react from that stance?!

19:43.870 --> 19:45.830
That was close, you bastard!

19:45.830 --> 19:47.500
But now it's my turn!

19:47.500 --> 19:49.630
Toe Kick-Style Back Knee Blast!

19:49.630 --> 19:50.590
TOE KICK-STYLE BACK KNEE BLAST!

19:51.710 --> 19:53.340
Don't you mess with me!

19:54.590 --> 19:56.630
You actually countered
instead of falling?!

19:56.630 --> 19:57.930
That's one hell of a balance.

19:57.930 --> 20:00.300
Right when I figured
I could land a combo, too.

20:00.300 --> 20:01.640
I see.

20:02.010 --> 20:03.930
I know well enough now.

20:03.930 --> 20:07.850
I'll never beat her
if I play with Armed Lava.

20:08.920 --> 20:10.690
Time out, Sunraku.

20:10.690 --> 20:13.400
Sorry, but let's pause this for now.
I want to talk—

20:18.610 --> 20:19.820
What?

20:22.220 --> 20:24.040
I didn't hear you that time, okay?

20:24.040 --> 20:27.080
It was an accident. You can't just
stop a jump kick out of the blue.

20:27.080 --> 20:28.120
Just laugh it off.

20:28.120 --> 20:30.500
This one doesn't count, okay?

20:30.500 --> 20:32.540
What?! A match is a match!

20:32.540 --> 20:33.340
Shut up!

20:33.340 --> 20:36.170
Hey, you are the one
who challenged me, you know?

20:36.170 --> 20:37.510
There, there.

20:37.510 --> 20:43.430
So, what was it that you wanted
to test by having Sunraku play as Metius?

20:46.220 --> 20:47.980
Watch this.

20:48.600 --> 20:53.440
The Galaxia Heroes: Burst World Tour
Championships from three years ago.

20:53.940 --> 20:58.530
The new hero from Japan, storming into
the scene with a string of wins, "K,"

20:58.530 --> 21:00.950
picked Armed Lava as expected!

21:00.950 --> 21:06.500
And likewise, the world champion,
Silvia Goldberg, picked Metius!

21:07.250 --> 21:08.960
ARMED LAVA VS. METIUS

22:39.800 --> 22:42.720
SLF Theater!

22:42.720 --> 22:43.510
#37 WHO IS KEI UOMI?
SLF Theater!

22:43.510 --> 22:44.970
#37 WHO IS KEI UOMI?
Mini!

22:44.970 --> 22:46.180
#37 WHO IS KEI UOMI?

22:47.010 --> 22:49.010
Tell us your name.

22:49.010 --> 22:49.930
It's Kei Uomi.

22:49.930 --> 22:52.640
KEI UOMI

22:52.640 --> 22:54.350
How old are you?

22:54.350 --> 22:56.150
I'm 19.

22:56.150 --> 22:58.060
You're so young.

22:58.060 --> 22:59.290
What's your job?

22:59.820 --> 23:01.110
I'm a pro gamer.

23:01.110 --> 23:03.400
What a wonderful job.

23:03.400 --> 23:05.570
A source of admiration for all gamers.

23:05.570 --> 23:07.620
It's not all that glamorous.

23:09.080 --> 23:10.290
What's your annual income?

23:10.290 --> 23:12.580
I think last year I earned...

23:12.580 --> 23:15.540
Wait, no, I'm not saying it.

23:15.540 --> 23:17.630
I'm sure you earned a lot.

23:17.630 --> 23:20.340
Well, I do earn a considerable amount.

23:20.340 --> 23:21.880
How much?

23:21.880 --> 23:23.340
I said I'm not saying it.

23:23.340 --> 23:27.390
Um, aren't you going to ask about
my favorite game or games I don't like?

23:27.390 --> 23:31.140
What fun is there in asking
such a basic question?

23:31.140 --> 23:32.310
Huh?

23:32.310 --> 23:33.330
So, your annual income?

23:34.230 --> 23:36.600
You're Sunraku, aren't you?

23:37.600 --> 23:38.900
I knew it!

23:38.900 --> 23:41.020
Changing your voice ain't gonna fool me!

23:41.020 --> 23:43.530
Looks like it's time.
If you excuse me now.

23:43.530 --> 23:45.070
Hey, wait!
